<section id="packages">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">How to work with us</p>
    <h2>Three packages. Fixed scope, fixed date.</h2>
    <p class="lede">No hourly billing, no retainers to start, no open-ended scope. Pick the one that
      matches where you are. Blueprint is the cheapest way to find out what a build actually costs
      &mdash; and it is credited back in full if you go on to build with us.</p>
    <p class="small muted">All prices below are our India sheet, in INR, exclusive of GST. If you
      invoice from outside India, ask on the call &mdash; you are quoted on our international sheet.</p>

    <div class="compare" aria-label="Packages at a glance">
      <a href="#blueprint"><span class="n">Blueprint</span><span class="p">&#8377;50,000</span><span class="d">1 week &middot; credited back if you build</span><span class="go">See what you get &darr;</span></a>
      <a href="#launchpad" class="core"><span class="n">Launchpad</span> <span class="tag">Most clients</span><span class="p">&#8377;4,00,000</span><span class="d">4 weeks &middot; one live web app</span><span class="go">See what you get &darr;</span></a>
      <a href="#buildout"><span class="n">Buildout</span><span class="p">&#8377;9,00,000</span><span class="d">8 weeks &middot; replaces the spreadsheets</span><span class="go">See what you get &darr;</span></a>
    </div>

    <!-- Blueprint -->
    <article class="pkg" id="blueprint">
      <div class="pkg-head">
        <span class="pkg-name">Blueprint</span>
        <span class="tag">Start here</span>
      </div>
      <p class="outcome">You walk away knowing exactly what will be built, what it costs and when it
        lands &mdash; with artifacts you own whether or not you hire us for the build.</p>
      <div class="meta">
        <div>Duration<b>1 week</b></div>
        <div>Price<b>&#8377;50,000</b></div>
        <div>If you build with us<b>Credited back in full</b></div>
      </div>
      <ul>
        <li>60-minute kickoff call plus up to 3 written Q&amp;A rounds.</li>
        <li>A clickable prototype of your core workflow &mdash; 4 to 8 screens.</li>
        <li>A written technical specification: data model, integrations, third-party services, named risks.</li>
        <li>A fixed-price, fixed-date build quote with acceptance criteria per deliverable.</li>
        <li>A 2-page handover so the artifacts are usable by any other developer.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="small muted"><b>Not included:</b> production code, a deployed app, a database, design or
        brand work, or any commitment from either side to proceed to a build.</p>
      <p class="accept"><b>Acceptance:</b> all five artifacts delivered by end of day 5, and you confirm
        in writing that the spec matches what you meant. The full fee is credited against a build started
        within 30 days.</p>
    </article>

    <!-- Launchpad -->
    <article class="pkg core" id="launchpad">
      <div class="pkg-head">
        <span class="pkg-name">Launchpad</span>
        <span class="tag">Most clients</span>
      </div>
      <p class="outcome">One working web application, live on the internet on a URL you own, that does
        the single job you hired us for &mdash; real users can sign in and complete the workflow end to end.</p>
      <div class="meta">
        <div>Duration<b>4 weeks from signed scope</b></div>
        <div>Price<b>&#8377;4,00,000</b></div>
        <div>After launch<b>14 days of defect fixes</b></div>
      </div>
      <ul>
        <li>One core workflow, up to 8 screens, up to 2 integrations from a pre-approved list
          (Stripe, Google or email sign-in, Sheets, Slack, email/SMS).</li>
        <li>Email and social login, one user role plus an admin view.</li>
        <li>Deployed to managed hosting, on your own accounts and your own domain.</li>
        <li>A demo on a live staging URL every Friday &mdash; four demos, four chances to correct course.</li>
        <li>Full source code in your repository, with a README another developer can follow.</li>
        <li>14 days of defect fixes after acceptance: anything that does not match the signed scope, fixed free.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="small muted"><b>Not included:</b> native iOS/Android apps (the web app is mobile-responsive;
        app-store builds are not included), scope added after signature, data migration off legacy systems,
        hosting or subscription fees, uptime guarantees or on-call.</p>
      <p class="accept"><b>Acceptance:</b> every item in the signed scope document demonstrated working on
        the production URL by the end-of-week-4 date.</p>
    </article>

    <!-- Buildout -->
    <article class="pkg" id="buildout">
      <div class="pkg-head">
        <span class="pkg-name">Buildout</span>
        <span class="tag">Replace the spreadsheets</span>
      </div>
      <p class="outcome">A multi-workflow internal system that replaces the spreadsheets and the manual
        copy-paste between your existing tools &mdash; with your team trained on it and 30 days of us
        standing behind it.</p>
      <div class="meta">
        <div>Duration<b>8 weeks from signed scope</b></div>
        <div>Price<b>&#8377;9,00,000</b></div>
        <div>After launch<b>30 days of support</b></div>
      </div>
      <ul>
        <li>Everything in Launchpad, scaled to 3 connected workflows, up to 20 screens, up to 4 integrations.</li>
        <li>Multiple user roles and permissions.</li>
        <li>A reporting dashboard with CSV export.</li>
        <li>One scheduled job &mdash; a nightly sync, a recurring report, reminder emails.</li>
        <li>Two 60-minute training sessions plus a written user guide.</li>
        <li>30 days of post-launch support: defect fixes plus up to 8 hours of small changes.</li>
        <li>A named weekly checkpoint with the founder, in writing.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="small muted"><b>Not included:</b> everything excluded from Launchpad, plus regulated-data
        work needing certification we do not hold (no HIPAA, SOC&nbsp;2 or PCI deliverables), re-writing a
        production system already carrying live customer traffic, scale engineering beyond ~100 concurrent
        users, and any integration without a documented public API.</p>
      <p class="accept"><b>Acceptance:</b> all three workflows demonstrated with your real data by the
        end-of-week-8 date, signed off one workflow at a time.</p>
    </article>

    <p class="small muted" style="margin-top:1.5rem">Ongoing maintenance exists as an add-on once we have
      built your app &mdash; business hours, two-business-day response, a fixed monthly allowance for small
      changes. It is offered at handover, not sold up front, and we keep only a small number of slots so
      that support never competes with a live build. <b>We do not promise uptime to anyone.</b></p>

    <p class="small" style="margin-top:1rem">Prices are fixed per package and exclusive of GST, confirmed
      against your written scope &mdash; one number, with the credit-back and the acceptance terms above
      attached to it. If the budget does not fit, the lever is scope: we drop a screen or an integration.
      The number does not move afterwards. Blueprint is credited back in full against a build started
      within 30&nbsp;days. Teams invoicing from outside India are quoted on our international sheet; ask
      on the call.</p>
  </div>
</section>
